==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ru|каранда́шъ}} {{ru-PRO}}

===Etymology===
In Russian from the 16–17th centuries. Borrowing from a {{der|ru|trk}} language. Compare {{cog|tr|karataş||black slate}}, composed of {{m|tr|kara||black}} + {{m|tr|taş||stone}}, {{cog|tt|кара таш||graphite, black lead}}. The origin of epenthetic {{m|ru||-н-}} is unclear. Perhaps it was added in colloquial Russian speech to ease the pronunciation. Compare {{m|ru|каланча́}} for the same epenthesis.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|каранда́ш}}
* {{audio|ru|Ru-{{PAGENAME}}.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|ru|aʂ}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|каранда́ш|adj=каранда́шный|dim=каранда́шик}}

# [[pencil]]
#: {{uxi|ru|У тебя́ есть '''каранда́ш'''?|Do you have '''a pencil'''?}}

